LUMA SUMMARY:
Naming and architecture session. The team moves from MMRC toward the QuackSink name, discusses what Opera/CDP is truly required versus historical habit, examines browser independence, and deals with the danger of sending huge source payloads through the live relay. The new project identity and the idea that QuackSink should become its own public system emerge here.
